  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for the details. Your account is active and is set to require a new password at sign-in, and we see no failed sign-in attempts or lockout, so you are not locked out. Please try this: on your Brightline laptop, sign in at the Windows sign-in screen (not a web page) while connected to the office network or VPN. Enter the temporary password, then choose a new password when prompted. The new password must be at least 14 characters and cannot be one you have used recently. Check that Caps Lock is off and watch for characters that look alike (l vs I, 0 vs O). If it still shows an error, please reply with the exact error text and whether you are on the office network, VPN, or home Wi-Fi, and the help desk will take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user: account active, not blocked, must_change_password=true, failed_login_count=0, sign_in_blocked=false, password_last_set 2026-10-11. check_signin_logs: 10 entries, all successful, no failed_password results, no hosting network, New York only; no lockout indicated. Device BL-LT-0112 online, last check-in 2026-10-11 03:22 UTC, 50.8% disk free, no warnings. Per KB-003 the first fix is the Windows sign-in screen on corporate network or VPN with the 14-character rule; I have not run unlock or reset since there is no lockout. KB-003 escalation condition (active with no change required) does not apply because must_change_password is true. Open items: the user's error text and sign-in location are unknown. Note the sign-in log timestamps (Sept 28 to Oct 9) predate the recorded password_last_set of Oct 11; worth a look if the error persists. If the user still cannot set a password, the next step is a new temporary password per KB-002 (not in the provided KB; search needed) or escalation to Tier 2.",
